      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Even VRChat has used AV1 in places before to reduce storage and bandwidth (when they published their new years stream recordings) so it seems logical to implement native support for it.\n\nIn addition to that it helps people with slower internet load videos faster along with helping people on limited connections save bandwidth.\n\nScratch the following since it would require that VRChat adds support for video and audio not being in a single file which is work they probably don't want.\n\nYouTube offers AV1 for more and more videos every day so you could set yt-dlp to prefer the Av1 video over the others which would just be the nice thing to do towards YouTube.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
